ACT ON THE ESTABLISHMENT AND OPERATION OF SUDOKWON LANDFILL SITE MANAGEMENT CORPORATION

Article 1 (Purpose)

The purpose of this Act is to promote the proper treatment of waste generated in the Seoul Metropolitan Area and its conversion into resources, and to contribute to creating a pleasant living environment for residents of areas surrounding the Sudokwon Landfill Site, by prescribing matters concerning the establishment and operation of the Sudokwon Landfill Site Management Corporation and thereby ensuring the efficient management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site.

Article 2 (Definitions)

The terms used in this Act are defined as follows:

1. The term “Sudokwon Landfill Site” means the regional waste treatment facility located in Oryu-dong, Wanggil-dong, Baekseok-dong, Gyeongseo-dong, and Geomam-dong in Seo-gu, Incheon Metropolitan City, and in Yangchon-myeon, Gimpo-si, Gyeonggi-do;
2. The term “Seoul Metropolitan Area” means areas within the jurisdiction of Seoul Special Metropolitan City, Incheon Metropolitan City, and Gyeonggi-do that deliver waste under the Wastes Control Act (hereinafter referred to as “waste”) to the Sudokwon Landfill Site.

Article 3 (Responsibilities)

(1) The State shall supervise the installation and management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site to ensure the proper treatment of waste generated in the Seoul Metropolitan Area and shall endeavor to promote the conversion of waste into resources.

(2) The Mayor of Seoul Special Metropolitan City, the Mayor of Incheon Metropolitan City, and the Governor of Gyeonggi-do (hereinafter referred to as the “Mayors/Do Governor”) shall ascertain the status of waste generation and treatment within their respective jurisdictions, endeavor to convert waste into resources and treat it properly, and cooperate in the proper management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site.

(3) The Mayors/Do Governor or the heads of cities, counties, or autonomous districts that deliver waste to the Sudokwon Landfill Site shall cooperate to ensure the smooth securing of cover materials necessary for landfilling and the implementation of resident support projects and other relevant activities.

Article 4 (Comprehensive Environmental Management Plan for the Sudokwon Landfill Site)

(1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall formulate a comprehensive environmental management plan for the Sudokwon Landfill Site (hereinafter referred to as the “comprehensive plan”) every five years to ensure the proper management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

(2) The comprehensive plan shall include the following matters:

1. Plans for the use of the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
2. Measures to promote the conversion of waste generated in the Seoul Metropolitan Area into resources;
3. Installation and management of pollution prevention facilities;
4. Matters concerning the financing of the construction and operation of the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
5. Projects to support residents of areas surrounding the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
6. Plans to reduce pollution in areas surrounding the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
7. Other matters deemed necessary for the proper management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site.

(3) When formulating the comprehensive plan, the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall hear the opinions of the Mayors/Do Governor and consult with the heads of relevant administrative agencies in advance. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 5 (Environmental Management Plan for the Sudokwon Landfill Site)

(1) The Sudokwon Landfill Site Management Corporation under Article 7 shall formulate an environmental management plan for the Sudokwon Landfill Site (hereinafter referred to as the “management plan”) every two years, including the following matters, and obtain approval from the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. The same shall also apply to amendments to approved matters: Provided, That this shall not apply to amendments to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

1. Status of the use of the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
2. Types and quantities of waste delivered to the Sudokwon Landfill Site and acceptance standards;
3. Matters concerning the execution of infrastructure construction works at the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
4. Matters concerning the conservation of the environment surrounding the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
5. Matters concerning the post-closure management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
6. Other matters concerning the management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site.

(2) When formulating the management plan, the Sudokwon Landfill Site Management Corporation under Article 7 shall consult with the Mayors/Do Governor in advance.

Article 6 (Relationship with Other Acts)

Except as provided in this Act, the installation and management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site and support for residents shall be governed by the Wastes Control Act and the Act on Promotion of Installation of Waste Disposal Facilities and Assistance, etc. to Adjacent Areas.

Article 7 (Establishment and Legal Personality of the Sudokwon Landfill Site Management Corporation)

(1) The Sudokwon Landfill Site Management Corporation (hereinafter referred to as the “Corporation”) shall be established to manage the Sudokwon Landfill Site in an environmentally safe and efficient manner.

(2) The Corporation shall be a corporation.

Article 8 (Offices)

(1) The location of the principal office of the Corporation shall be prescribed by its articles of incorporation.

(2) Where necessary for the performance of its duties, the Corporation may establish branches or offices at necessary locations following a resolution of the board of directors.

Article 9 (Articles of Incorporation)

(1) The articles of incorporation of the Corporation shall include the following matters:

1. Purpose;
2. Name;
3. Locations of offices;
4. Matters concerning business activities;
5. Matters concerning executive officers and employees;
6. Matters concerning the board of directors and the steering committee;
7. Matters concerning financial accounting;
8. Matters concerning capital;
9. Matters concerning amendments to the articles of incorporation;
10. Matters concerning methods of public notice;
11. Matters concerning the enactment, amendment, and repeal of rules and regulations;
12. Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree.

(2) Where the Corporation intends to amend its articles of incorporation, it shall obtain authorization from the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 10 (Registration of Incorporation)

(1) The Corporation shall be established upon registration of its incorporation at the location of its principal office.

(2) Matters necessary for the registration of incorporation of the Corporation under paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

(3) The Corporation may not assert a matter requiring registration against a third party until that matter has been registered.

Article 11 (Prohibition of Use of Similar Names, Etc.)

No person other than the Corporation under this Act shall use the name “Sudokwon Landfill Site Management Corporation” or any similar name.

Article 12 (Executive Officers)

(1) The Corporation shall have, as its executive officers, one president, not more than three directors, and one auditor.

(2) The president and auditor shall be appointed and dismissed by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

(3) Directors shall be appointed and dismissed by the president with approval from the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

(4) The term of office of the president shall be three years, and the terms of office of directors and the auditor shall be two years, and each may be reappointed for successive one-year terms. In such cases, the appointing and dismissing authority shall determine whether to reappoint them in consideration of their performance of duties under Article 13.

Article 13 (Duties of Executive Officers)

(1) The president shall represent the Corporation and exercise overall control over its affairs.

(2) Directors shall share responsibility for the Corporation’s affairs as prescribed by the articles of incorporation and, where the president is unable to perform duties due to unavoidable circumstances, shall act on behalf of the president in the order prescribed by the articles of incorporation.

(3) The auditor shall audit the affairs and accounts of the Corporation.

Article 14 (Restriction on the President’s Authority to Represent the Corporation)

With respect to matters in which the interests of the Corporation conflict with those of the president, the president shall not represent the Corporation, and the auditor shall represent the Corporation.

Article 14-2 (Appointment of Agents)

The president may appoint, from among the employees and as prescribed by the articles of incorporation, agents authorized to perform judicial or extrajudicial acts concerning the Corporation’s affairs.

Article 15 (Grounds for Disqualification of Executive Officers)

(1) No person who falls under any of the following shall become an executive officer of the Corporation:

1. A person who falls under any subparagraph of Article 33 of the State Public Officials Act;
2. A person who falls under Article 34 (1) 2 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions.

(2) Where an executive officer comes to fall under any subparagraph of paragraph (1), or is found to have fallen under any such subparagraph at the time of appointment, that executive officer shall automatically retire from office.

(3) Acts in which an executive officer who retires from office under paragraph (2) participated before retirement shall not lose their effect.

Article 15-2 (Restrictions on Concurrent Employment of Executive Officers and Employees, Etc.)

(1) Executive officers and employees of the Corporation shall not engage in any work for profit outside their official duties.

(2) The president and auditor of the Corporation may engage in nonprofit work outside their official duties with permission from the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, and directors and employees of the Corporation may do so with permission from the president. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 16 (Appointment and Dismissal of Employees)

Employees of the Corporation shall be appointed and dismissed by the president as prescribed by the articles of incorporation.

Article 17 (Deeming Persons Public Officials for Purposes of Applying Penalty Provisions)

Executive officers and employees of the Corporation shall be deemed public officials for purposes of applying Articles 129 through 132 of the Criminal Act.

Article 17-2 (Prohibition of Disclosure of Confidential Information, Etc.)

No current or former executive officer or employee of the Corporation shall disclose or misappropriate confidential information acquired in the course of duties.

Article 18 (Board of Directors)
(1) The Corporation shall have a board of directors to resolve important matters concerning its business.
(2) The board of directors shall consist of directors, including the president.
(3) The auditor may attend meetings of the board of directors and state opinions as necessary.
(4) Matters necessary for the operation of the board of directors shall be prescribed by the articles of incorporation.

Article 19 (Business Activities)
(1) The Corporation shall carry out the following activities:
1. Treatment of waste brought into the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
2. Installation and management of waste treatment facilities under subparagraph 8 of Article 2 of the Wastes Control Act and facilities ancillary thereto;
3. Installation and operation of facilities for recovering resources from waste;
4. Establishment of a residents support fund and provision of support to affected surrounding areas;
5. Determination and collection of the following:
(a) Waste acceptance fees necessary for treating waste brought into the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
(b) Surcharges under Article 8 of the Act on Promotion of Installation of Waste Disposal Facilities and Assistance, etc. to Adjacent Areas;
(c) Charges necessary for the installation of waste treatment facilities, collected from the Mayors/Do Governor, mayors, county heads, heads of autonomous districts, or persons who bring waste into the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
6. Environmental management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site and surrounding areas;
7. Installation and management of pollution prevention facilities;
8. Development and operation of borrow pits to secure soil and sand for use as cover material;
9. Post-closure management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
10. Installation and operation, within the Sudokwon Landfill Site, of park facilities under subparagraph 4 of Article 2 of the Act on Urban Parks, Green Areas, Etc., sports facilities under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Installation and Utilization of Sports Facilities Act, cultural facilities under Article 2(1)3 of the Culture and Arts Promotion Act, and other facilities;
11. Other duties entrusted by the State or local governments in connection with the establishment and management of the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
12. Duties incidental to the activities specified in subparagraphs 1 through 11, including surveys and research, technological development, design, responsible supervision, measurement and analysis of environmental pollutants, and technical support.
(2) Where necessary for the efficient performance of the activities specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1), the Corporation may, with the approval of the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, make equity investments in or contributions to businesses related to those activities. <Amended on October 1, 2025>
(3) The Corporation may, with the approval of the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, entrust the activities specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) to others. <Amended on October 1, 2025>
(4) Matters necessary for equity investments or contributions under paragraph (2) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 20 (Financial Resources for Business Activities)
The financial resources of the Corporation shall consist of the following funds:
1. Waste acceptance fees, surcharges, and charges under Article 19(1)5;
2. Subsidies from the State and local governments;
3. Earnings generated from the activities under Article 19;
4. Borrowings under Article 22;
5. Funds raised through the issuance of bonds under Article 23;
6. Other receipts.

Article 21 (Subsidies)
The State or a local government may provide subsidies for the Corporation’s business activities within budgetary limits.

Article 22 (Borrowing of Funds, Etc.)
The Corporation may, with the approval of the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, borrow funds necessary for carrying out the activities under Article 19, including borrowing from international organizations, foreign governments, or foreign persons. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

Article 23 (Issuance of Bonds)
(1) The Corporation may issue bonds with the approval of the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on October 1, 2025>
(2) When approving the issuance of bonds under paragraph (1), the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall consult in advance with the Minister of Finance and Economy. <Amended on October 1, 2025>
(3) Claims for the principal and interest of bonds shall be extinguished by prescription after 5 years and 2 years, respectively, calculated from the redemption date.
(4) Other matters necessary for the issuance of bonds shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 24 (Steering Committee)
(1) The Corporation shall have a steering committee (hereinafter referred to as the “Committee”) to deliberate on important matters concerning the activities under Article 19 before the board of directors adopts resolutions on such matters.
(2) The Committee shall consist of a chairperson and members.
(3) The president of the Corporation shall serve as chairperson, and the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall appoint or commission the following persons as members: <Amended on October 1, 2025>
1. 1 relevant public official recommended by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment;
2. 2 relevant public officials recommended by each of the Mayors/Do Governor;
3. 6 residents’ representatives recommended by residents of the areas surrounding the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
4. 1 relevant expert recommended by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, 1 relevant expert recommended by representatives of residents of the areas surrounding the Sudokwon Landfill Site, and 1 relevant expert recommended by the Mayors/Do Governor.
(4) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall not refuse to appoint or commission a member recommended under paragraph (3) unless there are special grounds for doing so. <Amended on October 1, 2025>
(5) Members shall not serve full-time.
(6) The terms of office of members under paragraph (3)3 and 4 shall be 2 years and may be renewed.
(7) The Committee shall deliberate on the following matters:
1. Waste acceptance fees for waste brought into the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
2. The types and volumes of waste brought into the Sudokwon Landfill Site, the criteria for accepting such waste, and the areas from which it may be accepted;
3. Matters concerning the installation of facilities and provision of support to preserve the environment surrounding the Sudokwon Landfill Site;
4. Other matters that the president of the Corporation deems necessary for deliberation and submits to a meeting of the Committee.
(8) Other matters necessary for the operation of the Committee shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 25 (Business Year)
The business year of the Corporation shall coincide with the fiscal year of the Government.

Article 26 (Approval of Business Plans, Etc.)
The Corporation shall prepare a business plan and draft budget for each business year and obtain the approval of the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, as prescribed by Presidential Decree. The same shall also apply when amending them. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

Article 27 (Submission of Statements of Accounts)
The Corporation shall prepare statements of accounts for each business year, have them audited by a certified public accountant designated by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, and submit them to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment by the end of February of the following business year. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

Article 28 (Guidance and Supervision of Business)
(1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall guide and supervise the Corporation with respect to the following matters: <Amended on October 1, 2025>
1. Matters concerning the proper performance of the Corporation’s activities under Article 19;
2. Matters concerning the proper performance of business activities directly related to affairs under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
(2) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may require the Corporation to report on matters concerning its business, accounting, and property or require public officials under the Minister’s authority to inspect the Corporation’s books, documents, and other objects. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

Article 29 (Application Mutatis Mutandis of the Civil Act)
Except as otherwise provided in this Act and the Act on the Management of Public Institutions, the provisions of the Civil Act concerning incorporated foundations shall apply mutatis mutandis to the Corporation.

Article 29-2 (Penalty Provisions)
Any person who, in violation of Article 17-2, discloses or misappropriates confidential information acquired in the course of duties shall be punished by imprisonment with labor for not more than 2 years or by a fine not exceeding 20 million won. <Amended on December 12, 2017>

Article 30 (Administrative Fines)
(1) An administrative fine not exceeding 1 million won shall be imposed on any person who violates Article 11.
(2) Administrative fines under paragraph (1) shall be imposed and collected by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

ADDENDA <Act No. 6200, Jan. 21, 2000>

Article 1 (Effective Date)

This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.

Article 2 (Establishment Committee)

(1) The Minister of Environment shall, within one month from the date of promulgation of this Act, appoint not more than 10 members to constitute an establishment committee and have it handle affairs concerning preparations for the establishment of the Corporation.

(2) The establishment committee shall prepare the articles of incorporation of the Corporation and obtain approval therefor from the Minister of Environment.

(3) Upon obtaining approval under paragraph (2), the establishment committee shall register the establishment of the Corporation.

(4) Upon completing the registration of establishment of the Corporation under paragraph (3), the establishment committee shall hand over its affairs and property to the president of the Corporation, and the members of the establishment committee shall be deemed released from their appointments upon completion of the handover.

Article 3 (Succession to Rights and Obligations)

The Corporation shall succeed comprehensively to the rights and obligations concerning the establishment and operation of the Sudokwon Landfill Site held, as at the time this Act enters into force, by the Sudokwon Landfill Site Operation and Management Association established under Article 149 of the Local Autonomy Act and the Environmental Management Corporation established under the Environmental Management Corporation Act.

Article 4 (Transitional Measures concerning Charges, etc.)

Costs borne, as at the time this Act enters into force, by the Mayors/Do Governor or a city mayor, county head, or head of an autonomous district for the establishment and operation of the Sudokwon Landfill Site and the acceptance and treatment of waste shall be deemed to have been collected and paid under Article 19, subparagraph 5.

Article 5 (Transitional Measures concerning the Sudokwon Landfill Site Operation and Management Association)

The Sudokwon Landfill Site Operation and Management Association established under Article 149 of the Local Autonomy Act and existing at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed dissolved under Article 154 of that Act on the effective date of this Act.

Article 6 (Transitional Measures concerning Waste Acceptance Fees)

Waste acceptance fees for waste brought into the Sudokwon Landfill Site established as at the time this Act enters into force shall be governed by the former provisions until such fees are determined under this Act.

